  "result": "Completion now handles arguments containing `#`. The cause was in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It splits the command line with `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default, so everything after a `#` was dropped.\n\nI set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character. Splitting `prog a#b #c d` now gives `['prog', 'a#b', '#c', 'd']`, and the 58 tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass. I didn't run the rest of the suite.\n\nI didn't add a regression test or a changelog entry, and nothing is committed.",
